                  },
                  "elements": []
                },
                {
                  "id": "70cebf5a",
                  "elType": "widget",
                  "widgetType": "text-editor",
                  "isInner": false,
                  "settings": {
                    "_title": "Copy",
                    "_css_classes": "gp-copy",
                    "editor": "<p>The project began with an existing cover direction, a supplied 33-page layout/manuscript and established story illustrations. The task was to bring those materials into a consistent cover and interior presentation, rather than create a new story or replace its illustrations.</p><figure class=\"gp-case-evidence\"><img src=\"{{asset:luma-cover-before-674.webp}}\" width=\"674\" height=\"900\" alt=\"Supplied earlier Luma cover direction before the redesign\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Earlier supplied cover direction reproduced from the case-study PDF, page 2. The final cover above shows the documented redesign.</figcaption></figure><p>The work needed to consider title and author hierarchy, front-to-back cover continuity, a readable back-cover copy area and a comfortable reading layout inside the book.</p>"
                  },
                  "elements": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
