                  "isInner": false,
                  "settings": {
                    "_title": "Subheading",
                    "_css_classes": "gp-subheading",
                    "title": "Design and formatting decisions",
                    "header_size": "h2"
                  },
                  "elements": []
                },
                {
                  "id": "af43ad16",
                  "elType": "widget",
                  "widgetType": "text-editor",
                  "isInner": false,
                  "settings": {
                    "_title": "Copy",
                    "_css_classes": "gp-copy",
                    "editor": "<p>The cover redesign connected the front and back through the book’s Sky Realm imagery. The title, character and author name were given a coordinated hierarchy. Back-cover copy was placed in a defined area that could be read against the artwork.</p><p>Inside the book, child-friendly typography, compact read-aloud lines and attention to the gutter supported the supplied text and illustrations. Ownership and title pages introduced the book before the story. Alternating text and illustration pages kept the visual presentation consistent.</p>"
                  },
                  "elements": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
